WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.003
I'm registered as an Arizona independent.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.005
I know some people might be a little bit

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.706
surprised by this, but

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.842
actually I think it makes a lot of sense.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.077
A growing number of Arizonans

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.013
and people like me

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:13.513
just don't

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.816
feel like we fit neatly into one party's

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.085
box or the other.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.421
Welcome back to State of the Union.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.889
That was Kirsten Cinema

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.090
explaining her decision

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.625
to change her party

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.360
from Democrat to independent.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.396
Let's talk about it with our panel.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.597
Good morning, everybody.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.466
Congressman, already you are

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.402
a member of Congress, is sitting

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.737
member of Congress, was in her party.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.273
One of your colleagues Congressman

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.410
Jamaal Bowman, tweeted the following

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.780
by Felicia after news broke about cinema.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.281
He's obviously he's a progressive.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.216
He's not upset to see her leave.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.486
Should Democrats get behind

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.754
an alternative

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.856
that's officially on the D column,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.824
like your

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.859
your colleague Ruben Gallego

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.294
will have a Democrat running?

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.295
I think what a lot of us

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.363
who represent

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.065
districts who got elected by Republicans

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.800
and independents and proudly

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.668
so as Democrats take issue with

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.537
is the idea that this is about principles

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:12.338
when it's really about politics.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.907
She was likely going to lose her

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.108
next primary

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.543
and that's why she's doing this.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.877
It's not a principled change.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.545
She's voted with us,

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.980
I think, 96% of the time.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.182
So it's not about that.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.116
It's about that.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.818
She saw the writing on the wall

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:25.452
politically.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.319
And so I think we'll have

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.154
a Democratic nominee

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.522
and I hope that she doesn't

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.624
try to play spoiler.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.525
And Kristen

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.960
Soltis Anderson, on that note,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.097
you are a pollster and, you know,

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:37.430
kind of

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.333
where the electorate is in Arizona.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.935
Could she play a spoiler

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.069
if there's

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.337
Kyrsten Sinema, a Democrat

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.572
and a Republican on the ballot?

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.706
Well, if you look at the exit polls

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:50.110
from 20, 22 in Arizona, 40% of Arizonans

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.177
who voted identified

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.412
themselves as independents.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.681
33% Republican. 27% Democrat.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.282
So if there was any state

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.050
where you could kind of

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.351
pull this off and be successful,

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.252
Arizona might be it.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.553
This is the state that gave us folks

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.422
like John McCain, Jeff Flake,

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.023
this maverick streak.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.125
The challenge she's going to face

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.526
is when she says

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.460
there are a lot of Americans

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.795
who don't identify with either party.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.863
They pick some form column

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.631
some of column B, she's right.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.866
But many of those Americans

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:13.800
don't necessarily

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.536
say want to see policies that support the

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.271
the rich and powerful, etc.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:18.671
And that's

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.306
what the allegations from her Democratic

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.774
opponents have often been.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.143
So there are lots of different ways

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.210
you can be an independent.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.278
It's not clear to me

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.447
that her particular recipe

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.582
will resonate a lot with Arizona voters.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.017
I totally agree with that.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.319
She doesn't fit the Angus King mold

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.288
or the Bernie Sanders mold.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.456
And I think she's going to be out

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:36.956
in the cold.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:37.924
This would have been a smarter

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.726
move for Joe Manchin,

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:40.760
where no Democrat

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.195
can be elected in West Virginia

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.630
than it is for her.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.831
Let's talk a bit about

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.366
Brittney Griner and

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.934
the remarkable release

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:49.903
she had to.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.037
25 excuse me,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:54.174
she was in prison and she was

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:56.242
released in an exchange with Victor Boot.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:59.078
25 year sentence is what he was serving,

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.147
and then he was set free.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:02.482
David Urban,

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.951
I know that you were trying to help

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.320
another person who is still held captive

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.290
in or in prison in Russia.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.091
Paul Whelan

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.526
get freed in the final years

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.961
of the Trump administration.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:15.895
What's your sense

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.965
knowing a bit about how all this works,

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.500
not just Brittney Griner,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.202
but the potential for Paul Wheeler?

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:22.969
First of all, I'd just say

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.772
congratulations to Roger Carstens.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.372
Who was assigned here

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.307
in the Biden administration

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.242
for the good work they did.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.510
None of this is very easy.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.111
The American people think it's

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.246
you know, it's an either or.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.214
They had a choice.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:34.914
They don't have a choice.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.050
You have to negotiate with the Russians.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.251
So think about Putin

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.219
sitting across the table

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.820
and Vladimir Putin

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.588
doesn't give you the choice.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.488
He said you can have this

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:43.690
or you can have nothing.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.257
So it was it.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.325
You could have Paul with Alison.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:47.193
We'd love to have Paul. We went home.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:47.994
I know his family would.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:48.995
I know Roger Carsons,

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.129
but I know the Biden administration

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:50.730
would like to have Paul.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.397
We went home

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.232
and they're going to get him home.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.166
But at this point in time,

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.400
they just couldn't get it done.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.135
And it's very difficult to do.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.604
It's not. It's not simply.

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.606
No, we don't want victory.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.140
We don't want Britney right now.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.841
We want Paul.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.743
That's all that wasn't even on the table.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.510
Yeah.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.312
I applaud what you just said.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.247
And it's also good

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.581
that Carson's is a holdover

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.816
from the last administration.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:12.352
This is not a political partizan job.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.020
I just want to amend my last comment.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.255
I meant that no Democrat

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:16.456
other than Joe Manchin.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:18.758
Sorry, Joe.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.760
Sorry. And just just give a quick plug.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.395
Rogers West Point by West Point

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.930
classmate and

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.100
and has done an incredible job and it was

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.434
well served as the Trump administration.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.403
But what about the argument that

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.972
Bob Menendez and others are making that

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.841
by doing this swap

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:36.242
with someone like Victor,

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.911
but that you are encouraging

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.380
and incentivizing

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.448
other bad actors from taking Americans?

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:44.617
Well, there's a risk of that.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:45.985
I don't think he's totally wrong,

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.487
but I think he's mostly wrong

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.121
because I think

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.656
we want to get Americans back.

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.224
And what really bothers me

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.726
is to see some people in whatever party

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.528
teeing off on this

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.462
when they should be

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.830
welcoming Americans back.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.098
And I do agree with David

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.733
totally that, first of all,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.468
the negotiator is highly skilled

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.636
and not a political actor.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.771
And second of all, what he got

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.339
done was heroic.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.807
Let me bring you in, Congressman.

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:08.041
All right.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:10.877
Because you are a fellow Baylor athlete

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.546
and I know you've been working

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.615
on this release What are your thoughts?

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.249
Well, we're

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.583
thrilled to have her home

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.785
in every meeting and briefing

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.486
that we have with Roger and his team.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.888
We also talked about Mr.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:22.288
Wheelan

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:23.990
and how we have to bring him home.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.325
And the White House has been very clear.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:25.925
And, you know,

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.026
I can say from my own,

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:28.261
you know, information is very clear

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.762
that there was no choice here.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.831
It was either bring Britney home or not.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:32.899
They were putting Paul wheeling

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:35.034
in a different bucket or treating him

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.669
as a spy, basically.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.236
And, you know,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.504
I think there's no reason for that.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.173
There's no evidence behind that.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.075
But that's why it's more difficult

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:42.542
to get him home.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.509
But we're going to keep working on

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.610
and I think he did a great job

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.745
in that interview with him.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.880
It seems to me that we have some hope

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.681
that we can bring him home.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.083
Yeah, more hope than I thought.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:50.316
Yeah.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:51.517
He said there are always cards,

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.252
which I thought was really interesting.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.020
I just want to quickly

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:54.687
turn to

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:55.521
what's going on

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.823
in the House of Representatives

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.925
and in your party in the GOP.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.128
The whole question of Kevin McCarthy,

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.830
whether or not

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.733
the Never Kevin group of Republicans

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.034
are going to

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:11.371
win the day and refuse to support him.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.506
I want you to listen to what he said.

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:16.209
This week about getting the votes

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:18.611
so, you know, you're having discussions

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.313
with these five members

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.181
of discussions with a lot of members.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.583
You have these five people.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:24.817
Are they open to

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:26.519
two coming over to your side?

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:29.288
I think a number of them are requesting

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:30.490
certain things and we're discussing.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.958
But the one thing most people

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:33.025
have to understand,

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.460
if one person wants something

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.061
that you have,

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:37.397
you have to have 218 within a conference

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.297
come together

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.601
He is in a very tough position,

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:42.735
but he benefits from the fact

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:44.137
that there is not a real

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:45.505
viable alternative.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:46.406
This is not a job

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:47.340
that everyone in the House

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.041
Republican Conference is clamoring for

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:50.510
is going to be a very,

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:51.911
very challenging two years

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.012
for whoever is elected

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.080
speaker of the House.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.581
And so to the extent that those

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:58.117
who are this sort of never Kevin group

00:06:58.351 --> 00:06:59.085
have not yet

00:06:59.085 --> 00:06:59.519
been able

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:00.319
to field

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:01.754
an alternative who could get

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.823
even a teeny tiny fraction

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.191
of the Republican conference,

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:06.793
I think it puts them in a very tough

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.461
the math is very challenging.

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:09.862
But he benefits greatly from the fact

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:10.863
that there is not

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.432
a great viable alternative.

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:13.399
You're the one at the table

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:14.634
who had to vote

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:15.501
in January

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:15.902
for Kevin

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.437
that will not be voting for Kevin.

00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:18.304
You heard it here first,

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:20.573
but if Republicans can't

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.909
come to a consensus, can you see yourself

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:26.012
voting for a bipartisan consensus

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:26.412
candidate?

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:27.847
Is that even you vote for a Republican?

00:07:27.847 --> 00:07:28.981
Come on. And Republicans.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:29.549
I'm a moderate.

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:30.716
I'd love to have

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:31.350
as the speaker

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.952
who could bring the whole House.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:34.320
Is there any Republican you can take?

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.121
I agree with Chris.

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.289
I don't think that there's a

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.623
you can't beat something with nothing.

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:38.925
I also say this.

00:07:38.925 --> 00:07:40.526
I think this is not a West Wing episode.

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:40.960
It's likely

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.562
that he's going to get the votes. Okay.

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:44.397
But he's going to be the weakest speaker

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:45.431
in modern history.

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:46.899
I think we're going to sorely missed

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:50.002
Nancy Pelosi and I think not even show.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.371
Well, I sorely missed Nancy Pelosi.

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:54.340
She kept the place going in it

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:56.342
and it made it much less of a circus

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:57.243
than it could become.

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:58.444
And I'm just saying,

00:07:58.444 --> 00:07:59.712
I wrote an op ed last week

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.347
that Joe Biden personally

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:02.381
could make a big difference

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:03.950
if he had office hours on the Hill

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.685
and tried to work with everybody

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:06.586
just to resolve

00:08:06.586 --> 00:08:07.286
and just remember

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:08.221
every single one of you,

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:08.488
you don't

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:09.555
have to be a member of the House

